    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c332456737993e0a22a7b314ce6021a905e3fd98b13621fc3a299d01ea0f311a",
      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast, then a full-day island tour with an English-speaking guide. Along the south coast, see unrestored platforms: Ahu Vaihu in Hanga Te’e Bay and Akahanga, said to be the burial place of the legendary king Hotu Matua. Continue to Rano Raraku, where most of the Moai were carved and many statues remain. Box lunch in nature. Visit Ahu Tongariki, restored with 15 Moai, then head to Ahu Te Pito Kura and the “Navel of the World”. Relax at Anakena Beach, with its warm turquoise water, white sand, palm trees and the Ahu Nau Nau platform. Return to Hanga Roa via the central route.",
